@pc0618 there's testbed data in europe-west4:

```py
from marin.datakit.sources import all_sources
from marin.datakit.normalize import NormalizedData
from marin.execution.artifact import Artifact

BASE = "data/datakit/sample/2026-05-26"

samples: dict[str, NormalizedData] = {
    src.name: Artifact.from_path(f"{BASE}/{src.name}", NormalizedData)
    for src in all_sources().values()
}
```

Since that data was produced more sources were added to `all_sources` - but I think you can just ignore those.

EDIT: updated to point at the 1T sample not the 10B.

🤖 Initial implementation and 5821 training plan update:

I added a 4915-style numeric-aware tokenizer variant to the tokenizer-sensitivity sweep. The implementation is a serializable HF `tokenizers` pretokenizer sequence:

1. isolate numeric runs from surrounding text;
2. cap numeric runs into chunks of at most 510 numeric characters;
3. apply right-aligned place grouping within each bounded chunk, so `1234567 -> 1|234|567`;
4. continue through the original upstream tokenizer pretokenizer.

This keeps the desired Singh/Strouse-style fixed-place grouping while avoiding the unbounded zero-width lookahead over arbitrarily long digit strings. For digit runs up to 510 characters, the splitter matches the original lookahead boundary behavior exactly; longer runs are bounded deliberately to avoid the pathological runtime described in the Arcee/Liu-style note.

Implemented experiment arms:

- `gpt-oss-place-digits`, initialized from `openai/gpt-oss-20b`
- `llama-place-digits`, initialized from `meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B`

These are explicit sibling arms to the existing learned controls (`gpt-oss`, `llama`), not silent replacements. They train the same 262,144-token base vocab, then derive 131,072 / 32,768 / 8,192 by BPE-rank truncation. Step hashes and metadata include the place-aligned digit policy so these artifacts remain distinct.

Submitted Iris prep run for the two numeric-aware HF arms on the same 50B-token-equivalent deterministic random Datakit subset used for #5821:

`/pc0618/tokenizer-sweep-5821-4915-place-digits-hf-50b-random`

Submission settings:

- dataset: `data/datakit/sample/2026-05-26`
- tokenizer train tokens: `50,000,000,000`
- sample mode: `random-shards`
- seed: `5821`
- families: `gpt-oss-place-digits,llama-place-digits`
- sizes: `262144,131072,32768,8192`
- region: `europe-west4`

Verification added locally:

- equivalence to the old lookahead splitter for digit-run lengths 1..510;
- isolation of contiguous digit runs from surrounding text;
- tokenizer pretokenizer serialization smoke test;
- 100k-digit uninterrupted string runtime guard.

Training/eval plan for crossing this off under #5821:

- finish the numeric-aware tokenizer prep run;
- retokenize the same 50B train cache and validation/holdout material for `gpt-oss-place-digits` and `llama-place-digits`;
- train the same fixed MoE architecture/budget as the current 5821 learned-tokenizer comparison;
- compare each numeric-aware arm against its same-family non-numeric control using BPB / `bpb_fixed`, per-domain and per-language metrics, plus numeric/arithmetic-heavy slices where available;
- report whether the 4915 policy materially changes MoE training/eval behavior without changing corpus, vocab-size ladder, training budget, or eval denominator.
